package testmain

// Package testmain writes the main tack test builds a package's tests
// with, and deals with what the compiler reports in it. It is a port of
// the Go compiler's package testmain, function by function, and writes
// the same file, byte for byte, and the same diagnostics; Go's
// testmain/doc.go documents what the file holds and why. What follows is
// where the port differs and why.
//
// Role in the pipeline. The loader, in test mode (see Loader.tests),
// reads a package's files and its test files, parses them, and calls
// main_source for one file more, before anything is resolved; it parses that
// file into the package as its last, named file_name, and loads what it
// imports, std/testing. The driver then sets the program's entry to its
// function (entry, ast.Program's entry_unit and entry_node), reports
// what clashes finds before any stage runs, and passes what the stages
// report through diagnostics.
//
// Names. Go's FileID is a file's name, so Go finds the generated file by
// its name, FileName; the port's FileID is an index (see package
// source), so generated finds the file named file_name in the Set once,
// and every function here takes its FileID. Go's Source takes the
// package and its files; the port's loader package cannot be imported
// here, since the loader calls main_source, so main_source takes the package's
// name, its import path and its trees.
//
// Input and output. main_source takes the package's name and import path,
// its trees, the Set the files are in, which gives each test's place,
// and -run's pattern and -v, and returns the Tack source of the
// generated main, exactly Go's. clashes and entry take the program and
// the FileID of the generated file, and diagnostics the stages'
// diagnostics, taken over, that FileID and that of the package's first
// file.
//
// Invariants. Every string in the generated file is a literal, each
// byte outside printable ASCII, and every " and \, written \xHH, so a
// name, a path or a pattern of any bytes reads back exactly. A test is
// every function, not a method, of a test file whose name starts with
// test_, in file order and then source order. Nothing here recurses;
// each function walks the trees' top-level declarations once.
